🚀 Week 3 – Day 1 String Class & Methods in Java ☕

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

The `String` class provides many built-in methods to manipulate text.

👉 These methods are widely used in:

* Input processing
* Validation
* Data formatting
* Coding interviews

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔤 1. Common String Methods

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 length()

Returns the number of characters.

```java id="m1"
String str = "Java";
System.out.println(str.length());   // 4
```

---

🔹 charAt()

Returns character at a specific index.

```java id="m2"
System.out.println(str.charAt(2));  // v
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 substring()

Extracts part of a string.

```java id="m3"
String text = "Programming";

System.out.println(text.substring(3));    // gramming
System.out.println(text.substring(0, 4)); // Prog
```

---

🔹 equals()

Compares string contents.

```java id="m4"
String a = "Java";
String b = "Java";

System.out.println(a.equals(b));   // true
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 equalsIgnoreCase()

Ignores uppercase/lowercase.

```java id="m5"
System.out.println("JAVA".equalsIgnoreCase("java")); // true
```

---

🔹 compareTo()

Lexicographically compares strings.

```java id="m6"
System.out.println("Apple".compareTo("Banana")); // negative value
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 contains()

Checks if substring exists.

```java id="m7"
System.out.println("Hello Java".contains("Java")); // true
```

---

🔹 startsWith() and endsWith()

```java id="m8"
System.out.println("Java Programming".startsWith("Java")); // true
System.out.println("file.txt".endsWith(".txt"));          // true
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 indexOf()

Returns first occurrence index.

```java id="m9"
System.out.println("banana".indexOf('a')); // 1
```

---

🔹 replace()

Replaces characters or text.

```java id="m10"
System.out.println("Java".replace('J', 'L')); // Lava
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 trim()

Removes leading and trailing spaces.

```java id="m11"
System.out.println("  Hello  ".trim()); // Hello
```

---

🔹 toUpperCase() / toLowerCase()

```java id="m12"
System.out.println("java".toUpperCase()); // JAVA
System.out.println("JAVA".toLowerCase()); // java
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 split()

Splits string into array.

```java id="m13"
String sentence = "Java is fun";
String[] words = sentence.split(" ");
```

---

📌 Complete Example

```java id="m14"
class StringMethodsDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "Java Programming";

        System.out.println(str.length());
        System.out.println(str.substring(5));
        System.out.println(str.contains("Java"));
        System.out.println(str.toUpperCase());
    }
}
```

